Subject: [PATCH] sysv: check msgrcv errors before decoding the reply

msgrcv leaves the receive buffer untouched when it returns -1. In particular,
a signal may interrupt a receive with EINTR before any reply has arrived.
Scanning that buffer for a message magic produces a spurious "payload not
recognized" diagnostic. Retry EINTR without decoding, and send other receive
errors to the existing error-reporting path. Keep the request's semaphore and
serial number across an interrupted receive.

Applies to fakeroot 2.1.4 (GPL-3.0-or-later).

--- a/communicate.c
+++ b/communicate.c
@@ -572,7 +572,12 @@ void send_get_fakem(struct fake_msg *buf)
       l=msgrcv(msg_get,
                &fm,
                sizeof(fm)-sizeof(fm.mtype),0,0);
-
+      if (l == -1) {
+        if (errno == EINTR)
+          continue;
+        break;
+      }
+
       ptr = (uint8_t *)&fm;
       for (k=0; k<16; k++) {
         magic_candidate = *(uint32_t*)&ptr[k];
